Case:     T33379.  The test-case database holds NO authored objective, NO step text, NO test
          data and NO expected result for this case.  Its single step is empty.  No authored
          authority exists beyond the title.
          The tester designed the objective and all 7 steps below from three sources: the
          title; the X960 TPS row 228 "Telnet Client(IPv4) = Yes"; and the DUT's own CLI
          surface, read with the `?` help before anything was sent (STEP 1).
          Objective (designed by the tester), in four parts.
          1. The AT-x960-56YSQ has a telnet client command with an explicit IPv4 form.
          2. That command sends real IPv4 TCP to port 23 from the DUT itself.
          3. It completes a telnet login to a real telnet server and runs commands there.
          4. It reports a failure when the far end refuses, when the user name is wrong, and
             when the TCP port is wrong.
