  => STEP 6 PASS: the PORT argument really chooses the destination port.  Port 2323 was
     refused at the same moment that port 23 on 10.38.22.98 was accepting, so the refusal is
     specific to the port and not to the host.  The explicit IPv4 form `telnet ip <host>`
     then completed a full session.  The far end's "Last login: Tue Oct 20 23:56:57 UTC 2026
     from 10.38.22.97" line shows that it remembers the earlier session and attributes it to
     the DUT.

STEP 7 -- the DUT's own telnet server stayed off for the whole case       PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The DUT carried `no service telnet` before the case, from its own flash:/default.cfg, and
  still carried it at the end:

awplus# show telnet
    Telnet Server Configuration
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    Telnet server                      : Disabled
    Protocol                           : None
    Port                               : 23

  => STEP 7 PASS: `service telnet` controls only the inbound server.  The telnet CLIENT of
     TPS row 228 works on a unit whose telnet server is switched off, so the two are
     independent.
